    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2bd34bff-6fa0-543b-9347-be54751118d2" activityNameId="2e4d12f3-fc21-50ef-ae57-34d75efbbb2d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Use, printer, laser jet, b/w, per kg printed paper</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Use, printer, laser jet, b/w, per kg printed paper
The laser jet printer use (b/w, office) is calculated via the active mode electricity consumption taken from literature information. The dataset includes the share of the printer production (assumed life span 4 years), the energy consumption for the different modes in the use-phase, the rail and road transport from factory to user, the toner usage as well as the benzene emissions for the printing of 1 kg of paper.;
UUID: 36e171cb-b911-3b53-bc35-65c45c82cc1c
Describes the use of a laser jet printer (monochrome) in an office. Calculated per 1 kg of printed paper. Swiss supply mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of printer and toner, which are represented in the individual subdatasets.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Manufacturers, literature and own assumptions. 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: Assumptions had to be made for the printer life span.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_36e171cb-b911-3b53-bc35-65c45c82cc1c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
